      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 28-year-old woman presented with 6 months of intractable left frontal headache that was proved to be due to an intracranial lesion. After successful surgical removal, it was found to be an intracerebral osteoma without a dural attachment. The literature of intracerebral osteoma is reviewed."},
